worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_worklog.md-135-- **Watcher v3** (`scratchpad/r3a/exp35_phase_i_watch_v3.sh`) — checks the argument count before expanding; binds the supervisor by pid + `/proc` start time parsed after the `comm)` field + cwd + the sha256 of its exact NUL-delimited argv (`70f7c4a3…`, equal to the launch log's recorded cmdline); requires an object with a `stop_latch` key and an array of chunk objects with a string state; a `grep` read error is an event. Smoke-tested read-only (waits on the live supervisor; a wrong argv sha, a state without `stop_latch`, an object-valued `chunks` and a wrong argument count each fire at once); v2 stopped and v3 armed for the E2 milestone (N = 4). It joins the next tooling review with this script.
